@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+EmitterBatch models the synchronous per-emitter collect/detach/reserve/
+initialize/Initial-copy/publication protocol with two contexts and capacity3.
+StartSelf and BeginPrewarm enter the same detached reservation path directly;
+PrewarmEmission composes its completed-batch interface and scopes serial/count
+restoration across honest caller Begin/render/End. Renderer exceptions before End
+are existing failed paths, not a new recovery guarantee. New EmitParticle callers
+must own the synchronous callback scope; all current emitter callbacks, StartSelf
+and BeginPrewarm were audited. Invalid finite/bounds inputs refuse before reserve.
+
+Simplification: reuse one reservation/initializer routine for emitter, initial and
+prewarm spawns; a nullable local age list owns only one emitter callback scope.
+No fake denominator, provider-specific count, persistent queue or new clock.
+Native prepared arithmetic/actual API tests cover data; bounded models do not
+execute native scheduling/random order. Original camera-distance/child scheduling
+code is deliberately retained, unlike the historical broad dependency image.
+Initializer exceptions are fatal to the owning helper result, not recoverable
+partial scene publication. Full normal/save/render parity remains separate.
